<refentry xmlns="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook" version="5.2" id="process_refeaturize">

	<refmeta>
		<refentrytitle>process_refeaturize</refentrytitle>
		<manvolnum>1</manvolnum>
	</refmeta>

	<refnamediv>
		<refname>process_refeaturize</refname>
		<refpurpose>re-project spike waveforms onto previously saved PCA eigenvectors.</refpurpose>
	</refnamediv>

	<refsynopsisdiv>
		<cmdsynopsis>
		<command>process_refeaturize</command>
		<arg choice="plain"><option>-p</option> <replaceable>pca-file</replaceable></arg>
		<arg choice="plain"><option>-w</option> <replaceable>waveformLength</replaceable></arg>
		<arg choice="plain"><option>-n</option> <replaceable>nChannels</replaceable></arg>
		<arg><option>-i</option> <replaceable>indices-file</replaceable></arg>
		<arg><option>-x</option></arg>
		<arg><option>-v</option></arg>
		<arg><option>-h</option></arg>
		<arg choice="plain"><replaceable>spk-file</replaceable></arg>
		</cmdsynopsis>
	</refsynopsisdiv>

	<refsect1>
		<title>Description</title>
		<para>
			<command>process_refeaturize</command> reads spike waveforms from a binary
			<replaceable>.spk.N</replaceable> file and projects them onto the principal
			component eigenvectors that were saved to a <replaceable>.pca.N</replaceable>
			file by <command>process_pca -e</command>.  The resulting feature values are
			written to standard output, one space-separated row per spike, without a
			leading count line or a trailing timestamp column.
		</para>
		<para>
			This tool is used internally by the klusters spike-realignment workflow.
			After <command>SpikeRealign</command> shifts spike waveforms in-place,
			<command>process_refeaturize</command> is called for each shifted spike to
			recompute its feature vector using the original PCA basis, so the
			<replaceable>.fet.N</replaceable> file remains consistent with the updated
			<replaceable>.spk.N</replaceable> file.
		</para>
	</refsect1>

	<refsect1>
		<title>Options</title>
		<variablelist>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>-p</option> <replaceable>pca-file</replaceable></term>
				<listitem>
					<para>
						Path to the <replaceable>.pca.N</replaceable> file written by
						<command>process_pca -e</command>.  Contains the channel count,
						waveform window parameters, per-channel means, and
						column-major eigenvector matrices for all channels.
						(Required.)
					</para>
				</listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>-w</option> <replaceable>waveformLength</replaceable></term>
				<listitem>
					<para>
						Number of samples per waveform in the spike file.  Must match
						the value used when <command>process_pca</command> was originally
						run.  (Required.)
					</para>
				</listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>-n</option> <replaceable>nChannels</replaceable></term>
				<listitem>
					<para>
						Number of channels in the spike file.  Must match the channel
						count stored in the <replaceable>.pca.N</replaceable> file.
						(Required.)
					</para>
				</listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>-i</option> <replaceable>indices-file</replaceable></term>
				<listitem>
					<para>
						Plain-text file containing 0-based spike indices to
						re-featurize, one per line.  If omitted, all spikes in the
						spike file are processed.  Providing a subset is efficient when
						only a small number of waveforms have changed (e.g. after
						selective spike realignment).
					</para>
				</listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>-x</option></term>
				<listitem>
					<para>
						Append per-channel peak values as extra features after the PCA
						components.  Mirrors the <option>-x</option> flag of
						<command>process_pca</command>.  If the original
						<replaceable>.fet.N</replaceable> was produced with
						<option>-x</option>, this flag must also be supplied here.
					</para>
				</listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>-v</option></term>
				<listitem>
					<para>
						Verbose output.  Prints PCA model parameters and spike counts to
						standard error before processing.
					</para>
				</listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>-h</option></term>
				<listitem>
					<para>Print help and exit.</para>
				</listitem>
			</varlistentry>
		</variablelist>
	</refsect1>

	<refsect1>
		<title>Output Format</title>
		<para>
			One line per requested spike, written to standard output.  Each line
			contains <replaceable>nChannels</replaceable> ×
			<replaceable>nComponents</replaceable> integer feature values separated by
			spaces, in channel-major order (all components of channel 0, then all
			components of channel 1, etc.).  If <option>-x</option> is specified,
			<replaceable>nChannels</replaceable> additional peak values follow.
			No header line is written and no timestamp column is appended; the
			caller is responsible for patching these rows back into the
			<replaceable>.fet.N</replaceable> file at the correct positions.
		</para>
	</refsect1>

	<refsect1>
		<title>PCA File Format</title>
		<para>
			The <replaceable>.pca.N</replaceable> file written by
			<command>process_pca -e</command> contains a fixed header followed by
			per-channel mean vectors and eigenvector matrices:
		</para>
		<itemizedlist>
			<listitem><para><type>int32</type> magic — 0x50434145 (<literal>"PCAE"</literal>)</para></listitem>
			<listitem><para><type>int32</type> version — 1</para></listitem>
			<listitem><para><type>int32</type> nChannels</para></listitem>
			<listitem><para><type>int32</type> data2use — samples per channel used in PCA</para></listitem>
			<listitem><para><type>int32</type> nComponents — principal components kept</para></listitem>
			<listitem><para><type>int32</type> recShift — first sample offset within the waveform window</para></listitem>
			<listitem><para><type>int32</type> isCentered — 1 = centred projection; 0 = raw</para></listitem>
			<listitem>
				<para>For each channel: <type>double[data2use]</type> per-channel mean, followed by
				<type>double[data2use × nComponents]</type> eigenvectors in column-major order
				(column = component).</para>
			</listitem>
		</itemizedlist>
	</refsect1>

	<refsect1>
		<title>Exit Status</title>
		<variablelist>
			<varlistentry>
				<term>0</term>
				<listitem><para>Success.</para></listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term>1</term>
				<listitem>
					<para>
						Error: missing required arguments, could not open a file, bad
						magic in the PCA file, channel count mismatch, or I/O error
						during processing.
					</para>
				</listitem>
			</varlistentry>
		</variablelist>
	</refsect1>

	<refsect1>
		<title>See Also</title>
		<para>
			<citerefentry><refentrytitle>process_pca</refentrytitle><manvolnum>1</manvolnum></citerefentry>,
			<citerefentry><refentrytitle>process_mergefeatures</refentrytitle><manvolnum>1</manvolnum></citerefentry>
		</para>
	</refsect1>

</refentry>
